  "unit": "u07-directions",
  "title": "Places in town",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Mosques (**মসজিদ**) are everywhere in Bangladesh and make great landmarks: **মসজিদের সামনে** 'in front of the mosque'. Hindu temples (**মন্দির**) are common too, especially in older neighbourhoods.\n\n'Live' (in a place) is **থাকা**: **আমি শহরে থাকি** 'I live in the city', **আমার নানি গ্রামে থাকেন** 'My grandmother lives in the village' — note the polite **-েন** ending for an elder.\n\n**আছে** at the end of a sentence means 'there is': **মসজিদের সামনে একটা দোকান আছে** 'There's a shop in front of the mosque'.\n\n**Culture:** most city families still have a **গ্রামের বাড়ি** (village home) they return to for Eid.",
